! final.md — hand-back, 2026-11-04

Verbatim scratch record `.lares-scratch/seat-harness/luna14/final.md` (hand-back, file date 2026-11-04); only Markdown transliterated to memetic-wikitext, its words kept as written. Index: [[workshop index|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/workshop/seat-harness/luna14/index]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

* ''HIGH — `tools/launch-codex.mjs:418–424, 460`:'' The supervisor treats any bwrap exit as a normal seat exit. If bwrap fails before starting Codex—for example, if PID namespace creation is denied—the supervisor can still write `done-*` and return success. `HAVE_BWRAP` only probes a basic bind-and-run at `tools/seat-walls.mjs:52–53`; it does not prove this containment command works. Check the child’s exit result and distinguish setup failure from a completed seat.

* ''HIGH — `tools/launch-codex.mjs:448–451`:'' If `copyBack` throws after copying only some files, the catch leaves `copied` empty and the supervisor still writes the done marker. A waiter can see “done” while the hand-back is incomplete, contrary to the marker’s guarantee.

* ''MED — `tools/launch-codex.mjs:410–419, 447–453`:'' If the supervisor crashes or is killed, `--die-with-parent` can end bwrap, but nothing writes the completion marker. The documented `until [ -f done-* ]` wait can therefore hang indefinitely. Provide a crash-visible completion or failure path.

<<~/ahu>>

